      "writtenOn": "2023-10-06T16:08:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Shouldn\u0027t you be checking for when 0 bytes are available to read?\n\nAlso, I think this needs to be inside the loop above, or perhaps inside `VsockStream::recv`. Otherwise you\u0027ll still have the same issue if `read_exact` is called with a large buffer.",
      "revId": "906f26100c84eeadbb5973fb1940d003dcccee1f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c735756f_06870a20",
        "filename": "rialto/src/communication.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 183,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-09T08:19:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Shouldn\u0027t you be checking for when 0 bytes are available to read?\n\nChecking for 0 bytes availability does not work in this case. When the host sends a chunk of 1024 bytes to the guest VM, the receive buffer immediately becomes full, with 0 bytes available. Sending an update to the host at this point serves nothing, as the buffer allocation is already full and the `fwd_cnt` is 0. We need to send an update when the buffer is empty after we read everything, where we have `fwd_cnt` \u003d\u003d `buf_alloc`. This way, the host will know that we are ready to receive again upon receiving this message.",
      "parentUuid": "39fe3b61_50845fae",
      "revId": "906f26100c84eeadbb5973fb1940d003dcccee1f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7626ec1b_01975833",
        "filename": "rialto/src/communication.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 183,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-09T09:01:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, if the receive buffer is full then there are 1024 bytes available to read. When the buffer is empty there are 0 bytes available to read.",
      "parentUuid": "c735756f_06870a20",
      "revId": "906f26100c84eeadbb5973fb1940d003dcccee1f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
